{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/ofy9wn61","slideIndex":2,"text":"Introduce the setting: a fixed chest X-ray gallery and a fixed query set, with the target pathology becoming progressively less prevalent. This concerns evaluation-time gallery composition rather than class balance in the training data.\n\nSource: supplied Chest_XRay_Retrieval_IEEE_Format.docx. Reference numbers follow the manuscript."}
{"kind":"slide","id":"sl/jyx0ra1s","slideIndex":3,"layout":{"id":"ly/3yt8jipk","name":"ICAST Content"},"title":"Background and Problem Statement","textShapes":3,"backgroundColor":"rgba(250,250,250,1)"}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/1cj2d8b6","slideIndex":3,"position":{"left":120,"top":0,"width":1040,"height":104.57},"name":"Text 1","placeholder":"title","text":"Background and Problem Statement","geometry":"rect","style":{"fontSize":48,"typeface":"Roboto","color":"#FFFFFF","alignment":"center"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/0ba143al","slideIndex":3,"position":{"left":57.6,"top":148.8,"width":1164.48,"height":480},"name":"Text 1","placeholder":"body","text":"Retrieval returns similar prior chest X-rays for education and reference.\nPrior work studies embeddings and scarce or imbalanced categories.\nBalanced index-size experiments preserve the target class proportion.\nThis study fixes gallery size and reduces target prevalence from 5% to 0.5%.","geometry":"rect","style":{"fontSize":26.67,"typeface":"Roboto","color":"#333333","alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/r29obap4","slideIndex":3,"position":{"left":1173.52,"top":23.04,"width":58.48,"height":58.48},"name":"Slide Number","placeholder":"slideNumber","text":"4","geometry":"ellipse","fillColor":"#FFFFFF","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":24,"typeface":"Roboto","color":"#0B2545","bold":true,"alignment":"center"}}
{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/jyx0ra1s","slideIndex":3,"text":"Denner et al. [1] varied the number of indexed examples per class in a balanced index, changing absolute support while preserving prevalence. Rare and imbalanced settings also appear in SISH [2] and volumetric retrieval [4]. The present narrative review identified a gap in controlled multi-level prevalence reductions with queries and representations held fixed. The comparison with prior work is conceptual, not a numerical cross-study benchmark.\n\nSource: supplied Chest_XRay_Retrieval_IEEE_Format.docx. Reference numbers follow the manuscript."}
