{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/lwritgvq","slideIndex":6,"position":{"left":1173.52,"top":23.04,"width":58.48,"height":58.48},"name":"Slide Number","placeholder":"slideNumber","text":"7","geometry":"ellipse","fillColor":"#FFFFFF","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":24,"typeface":"Roboto","color":"#0B2545","bold":true,"alignment":"center"}}
{"kind":"table","id":"tb/bm98jid4","slideIndex":6,"position":{"left":57.6,"top":158.4,"width":1164.48,"height":357.12},"name":"Table 0","rows":6,"cols":2,"preview":"Item | Details"}
{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/gnmp4jqx","slideIndex":6,"text":"CNN-PT: supervised ImageNet ResNet-50 without adaptation. CNN-Common: normal/pneumonia/COVID-19 classification. CNN-NIH: NIH multi-label classification. SwAV-PT: ImageNet self-supervised SwAV without adaptation. SwAV-CLS: the same NIH classification objective as CNN-NIH, from SwAV. SwAV-SupCon: weighted multi-label supervised contrastive adaptation from SwAV. All provide 2,048-D backbone embeddings. SupCon uses two views of 64 source images, label-set Jaccard weights, temperature 0.07 and a training-only projection head. AdamW learning rate and weight decay are 0.0001, with up to 50 epochs and early stopping. Checkpoint selection uses objective-specific validation losses. Five gallery seeds measure gallery resampling, not independent retraining. Available fine-tuning annotations exclude target labels, but this does not verify clinical absence of targets in every image.\n\nSource: supplied Chest_XRay_Retrieval_IEEE_Format.docx. Reference numbers follow the manuscript."}
