{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/fu1gfa1s","slideIndex":7,"text":"The chart shows an unweighted arithmetic mean of the three pathology means at 0.5% target prevalence for four selected conditions, calculated from manuscript Table 2. Values: CNN-PT 0.0210; SwAV-PT 0.0275667; SwAV-CLS 0.0251333; SwAV-SupCon 0.0386. The display rounds to four decimals. CNN-Common and CNN-NIH were also evaluated, as listed in the setup table. The chart presents descriptive means, not a pooled inferential comparison. The claim of ten significant contrasts refers to query-paired SwAV-SupCon versus SwAV-CLS tests across all twelve pathology-prevalence conditions, globally Holm-corrected within 72 planned model comparisons. Exceptions: cardiomegaly at 0.5% and 1%. The strongest low-prevalence absolute P@10 values are 0.0163, 0.0335 and 0.0660 for cardiomegaly, emphysema and pneumothorax. Their enrichment over random expectation 0.005 is 3.26, 6.70 and 13.20 times. Pneumothorax is a cross-source condition and these means do not establish clinical utility.\n\nSource: supplied Chest_XRay_Retrieval_IEEE_Format.docx. Reference numbers follow the manuscript."}
