{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/udsvah03","slideIndex":8,"text":"The first displayed range rounds the manuscript relative P@10 loss range 83.4%-91.9% to whole percentages. All eighteen model-pathology endpoint contrasts show significant decline for both P@10 and nDCG@10 after Holm correction, adjusted p ≤ 2.30e-26. Absolute P@10 losses range from 0.0959 to 0.3480. SwAV-SupCon has the highest mean P@10 at all twelve pathology-prevalence conditions. Ten of its twelve planned contrasts against SwAV-CLS survive global correction. At 0.5%, adjusted p-values for SupCon versus CLS are >0.99 for cardiomegaly, 5.34e-7 for emphysema and 3.17e-6 for pneumothorax. A larger absolute loss can accompany better endpoint retrieval: on pneumothorax, SupCon loses 0.3480 versus CLS 0.2841, while remaining higher at both endpoints.\n\nSource: supplied Chest_XRay_Retrieval_IEEE_Format.docx. Reference numbers follow the manuscript."}
{"kind":"slide","id":"sl/m90b6t0r","slideIndex":9,"layout":{"id":"ly/3yt8jipk","name":"ICAST Content"},"title":"Conclusion and Future Work","textShapes":3,"backgroundColor":"rgba(250,250,250,1)"}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/xc3mho32","slideIndex":9,"position":{"left":120,"top":0,"width":1040,"height":104.57},"name":"Text 1","placeholder":"title","text":"Conclusion and Future Work","geometry":"rect","style":{"fontSize":48,"typeface":"Roboto","color":"#FFFFFF","alignment":"center"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/cbu58j2h","slideIndex":9,"position":{"left":57.6,"top":148.8,"width":1164.48,"height":480},"name":"Text 1","placeholder":"body","text":"Conclusion\nLower prevalence reduces retrieval quality across every evaluated model.\nOne training run and source confounding limit the SupCon finding.\nFuture work\nRepeat training and strengthen controls across dataset sources.\nTest lower target counts and obtain clinician-assessed relevance.","geometry":"rect","style":{"fontSize":26.67,"typeface":"Roboto","color":"#0B2545","bold":true,"alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/25kv2h0f","slideIndex":9,"position":{"left":1173.52,"top":23.04,"width":58.48,"height":58.48},"name":"Slide Number","placeholder":"slideNumber","text":"10","geometry":"ellipse","fillColor":"#FFFFFF","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":24,"typeface":"Roboto","color":"#0B2545","bold":true,"alignment":"center"}}
{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/m90b6t0r","slideIndex":9,"text":"Conclusions concern the evaluated ResNet-50 conditions, three targets and prevalence protocol. Single checkpoints do not estimate retraining variation. Classification and SupCon checkpoints use objective-specific selection criteria. SIIM supplies pneumothorax queries and NIH supplies relevant gallery images, aligning source with retrieval role. Labels are imperfect, and external metadata cannot establish exhaustive finding annotations. Zero-shot therefore means target labels were absent from available adaptation labels. No radiologist judged relevance or diagnostic benefit. The lowest prevalence still has 100 relevant images; much larger approximate indexes and lower absolute counts remain untested. Report at least two clinically relevant gallery-prevalence levels.\n\nSource: supplied Chest_XRay_Retrieval_IEEE_Format.docx. Reference numbers follow the manuscript."}
